              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hervorheben — \"to bring out, to single out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Im Bericht hebt die Lehrerin hervor, dass meine Tochter sehr fleißig ist. In the report the teacher singles out how hard-working my daughter is."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Separable and strong: sie hebt hervor, sie hat hervorgehoben. Literally to lift something out to the front."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hervorheben is built from hervor \"forth, out\" and heben \"to lift\", inherited from Old High German heffen (EtymDB): you lift a point out so that everyone notices it."
            }
          ]
        },
